#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27635777-a8dd-5afe-a296-ee402af7fe39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422764} {:answer/id #uuid "480417bf-3b78-555e-8194-c8ef38995e34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422789} {:answer/id #uuid "6f580ecb-7efc-5512-9398-273631dd1bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422819} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa72215-7cb2-51f3-b5db-2adac83c439f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422832} {:answer/id #uuid "b0260bc6-012f-5b9c-a80e-93287d27b6c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y\\le 3 \\\\ y\\ge 2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422880}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422764} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c5be21f-60e7-597b-83dc-3c20339aa469" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "262609c0-5557-5285-b43c-f82fdb8825a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-90054" :question/problem "![](images/b8/b8c1d5902a76a68e5f8358d4c3668e1be184ec7241184df4ff1363d41995f3aa.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $x+y=3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-x+3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\"  inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+3,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+y>3.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict.  Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21f1cf91-2163-5bf5-8bdd-17c06cfb56f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422757} {:answer/id #uuid "49247309-afac-5793-a965-e29d26e684cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422792} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff44b6f-7f18-5b59-b687-6bfafa9923c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y<\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422848} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b98254-dc2c-5569-ba7c-775a46563922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422893} {:answer/id #uuid "fbeae658-1ad6-5399-b8e3-d95d56f3c62b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422926}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422926} :answer-field/id #uuid "94914b35-e16f-5398-9a50-4baddb153e6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "66b0d8c5-2487-53cc-b840-b06edcc12d56" :question/math-academy-id "q-90323" :question/problem "![](images/e8/e863789ff989ee1cb3d3fe6c22fe0d4daa1dac76d6fbfbebdad801006ca4c969.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=4x+3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<4x+3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{4}x-2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8760f28c-314a-5353-a151-1773d06194c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\le -x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422840} {:answer/id #uuid "a6ae492d-6998-592e-aad4-9e4158c3d62a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422871} {:answer/id #uuid "d086efec-878a-5d60-959f-69c0d1d6a64c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y<-x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422900} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc950a4-a4b3-574a-9a32-22ca9de0541d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422910} {:answer/id #uuid "ea85fa77-5fe3-59b1-a642-7a3377ab8ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422917}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422917} :answer-field/id #uuid "f86fe5f2-d23c-5598-bb24-07f9f597ec1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3e5e2c49-2afd-5324-972b-43974f8bfdd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-90327" :question/problem "![](images/76/762e53967ddb3ccddfa1c9b7a2aa303d66fc1b761c9be8f409c0b91ecb0201de.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b4c000b-c921-5509-a96b-cb9f0d93c9ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406895} {:answer/id #uuid "670ba1f9-ed3f-5406-a924-34d394e42af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406897} {:answer/id #uuid "8f9616d5-ee83-53e1-8dc5-492827d8a46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406901} {:answer/id #uuid "90f92edc-d0c5-5a32-ba22-e172277f28a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406902} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c1b6f1-8629-5f1d-8828-dbc4c3ad5ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406910}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406902} :answer-field/id #uuid "97997922-270d-5956-b157-409ccbb997d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "77d8a3b9-ab3f-5af1-ac16-cd6ceeb35611" :question/math-academy-id "q-87213" :question/problem "Compute $P(1<X\\le 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{18}x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X\\le 5) & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{18}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{36}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407297 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d785f01e-c01b-508b-a7e4-0b68e3819afd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473512} {:answer/id #uuid "72475eb4-0b35-5d4b-9ea7-4c75ae1d9bdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473513} :answer-field/id #uuid "7063df18-38c8-5001-85dc-c37c2a884180" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A$ $={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,$ $\\,$ where $R=[-3,2]\\times [0,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45915786-bde2-58ed-b09f-01d02dd4ab1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473514} {:answer/id #uuid "db2767a5-0290-566a-8860-446c19d11819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473515}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473514} :answer-field/id #uuid "9428d01a-a858-5759-ad6e-dec6825a2e03" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{R}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A$ $={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,$ $\\,$ where $R=[-5,5]\\times [0,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474152} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20decd90-c71f-5b9c-af2d-3a173c83d963" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473516} {:answer/id #uuid "025119c3-228a-5031-89d8-d102fe48b0f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473517}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473516} :answer-field/id #uuid "31799862-7294-50e6-9e5a-cbd879317060" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A$ $={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,$ $\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ed965e5b-f0df-5c0f-9c7c-0cb7a433c067" :question/math-academy-id "q-86866" :question/problem "![](images/51/51706be38cc1c72079fe702c899b575ea53ba4d85e7990a6aa81f20dc8da4de3.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle ={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$ $\\,$ where $R=[-3,2]\\times [0,3]$” is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{R}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle ={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$ $\\,$ where $R=[-5,5]\\times [0,3]$” is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle ={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$ $\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$” is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle ={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$ $\\,$ where $R=[-3,2]\\times [0,3]$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37e80d1f-a6cc-56c6-b6b7-fa5a674e76b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-4,-3,0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422942} {:answer/id #uuid "64f88695-0ba2-5bd2-8bb5-18e4d44b8fa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-1,0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422947} {:answer/id #uuid "6fae85ef-71a7-5f26-97c5-d52da8886bb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-3,-1,0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422948} {:answer/id #uuid "b136f681-32a7-5eb5-9e00-9e37fd18a10f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-4,0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422951} {:answer/id #uuid "eac455f6-1921-5f10-b49f-0fbffba0ec40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{-3,-2,-1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422955}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422951} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f37bd0-557b-529a-88f6-615287ca253d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3574e15c-1d81-5d76-a394-37484fa9dfbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-174363" :question/problem "![](images/ae/aeb0c87a33cf30494636f0a8f8d411033ba064385ad04065abff184752ea99d7.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the subset $A$ of $U=\\{-4,-3,-2,-1,0\\}$ whose indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ is shown above?" :question/worked-solution "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the diagram above, only the elements $-4$ and $0$ are mapped to $1.$ Therefore, the indicator function in the diagram above corresponds to the set $A=\\{-4,0\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d7b4811-3743-5f1c-befb-52377f1ba995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{a,c,e\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422941} {:answer/id #uuid "5a8625f8-e0d2-5655-8966-249f3aefa53c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{a,b,c\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422946} {:answer/id #uuid "82a661df-e47f-572a-8fd4-59c67535d1c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{b,c,e\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422949} {:answer/id #uuid "a9aae1cf-ddff-5d29-9236-9f2621086282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{d,c,d\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422950} {:answer/id #uuid "e098f432-8d04-5972-83c4-4a6611dad8b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{a,d\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422953}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422949} :answer-field/id #uuid "72880716-881b-572f-a482-436f0d9e99ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a66f5e5d-805e-5011-9534-19a9e92d3193" :question/math-academy-id "q-174359" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c60072882a6effae61da543bfddff1053ab0bcc924d12c49f5acd697b0871c4.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the subset $A$ of $U=\\{a,b,c,d,e\\}$ whose indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ is shown above?" :question/worked-solution "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the diagram above, only the elements $b,c$ and $e$ are mapped to $1.$ Therefore, the indicator function in the diagram above corresponds to the set $A=\\{b,c,e\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d0bed3-2f44-5147-8b11-1799b1a77a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410207} {:answer/id #uuid "164c9de6-1afb-5748-ad52-794c0b12deda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410219} {:answer/id #uuid "2ed70e6b-a2cd-51da-96fd-f5a213dd7fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410239} {:answer/id #uuid "7db5c39d-db73-5155-8d2f-1ed953fb569c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410282} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9f5533-060f-5f5e-99fa-71a91f1849d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410207} :answer-field/id #uuid "b124b7e8-f665-5416-a587-c5c709c95b52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "803f66d6-b1cb-5f24-9bcd-afd86a0fb084" :question/math-academy-id "q-143802" :question/problem "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}, & x=0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}].$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each cubed value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{1}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{2}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{4}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e9019fa-53e3-5da4-b1e0-9f5b7131cd05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410213} {:answer/id #uuid "7465856e-9a5d-527e-9054-c95c24ffdaef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410278} {:answer/id #uuid "c5cac1e7-f645-5ed2-9530-e49763a8397e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410338} {:answer/id #uuid "cc721ea0-7d36-594b-a9cd-3c0139aedbbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410342} {:answer/id #uuid "f50e6a52-629e-5669-b331-2a7ee1fc70ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410366}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410342} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc02869c-5264-53f2-a4f6-8cbf93737163" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "81c0e5cb-c8d5-5dbe-9be3-3283a12b1fd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-347435" :question/problem "Consider the function\n\n$$\np(x)=1[x\\ge 0]\\cdot {x}^{2}+1[-3\\le x<0]\\cdot 1+1[x<-3]\\cdot (-2x).\n$$\n\nWhat is $p(-5)?$" :question/worked-solution "The indicator function $1[P]$ equals $1$ if the predicate $P$ is true and $0$ if $P$ is false.\n\n$$\n1[P]=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is true}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }P\\text{ is false}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5,$ we evaluate each indicator function:\n\n- $1[x\\ge 0]=1[-5\\ge 0]=0$ (since $-5\\ge 0$ is false)\n\n- $1[-3\\le x<0]=1[-3\\le -5<0]=0$ (since $-3\\le -5$ is false)\n\n- $1[x<-3]=1[-5<-3]=1$ (since $-5<-3$ is true)\n\nSubstituting into the expression for $p(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(-5) & =0\\cdot 25+0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-2(-5)) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the indicator functions act as a \"switch\": since $x=-5<-3,$ only the third term contributes to the result."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "964c5bc4-7a2e-5bae-85a7-d482c6e36e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411756} {:answer/id #uuid "a758ee1c-9dab-5058-8a43-ffb91581708b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411765} {:answer/id #uuid "c3bca5a5-b1a9-54bd-8c07-941077c325cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411785} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b6fede-844a-5216-ae74-664077e8f2bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411805} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b661e8-65e7-5407-8292-c4496fc2965b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411812}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411805} :answer-field/id #uuid "dee10a7b-d9ae-5a81-b136-732cb3456d2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1994bb13-7165-5891-a83f-5e7560b1da72" :question/math-academy-id "q-147946" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}(x+{y}^{2}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{4}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{9}{16},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}y[\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}-\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{9}{16}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411871 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c35ea81-1fba-5743-bc51-d55ebe9293ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411702} {:answer/id #uuid "4668fa6c-efd9-5349-af00-60d3491fb89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411715} {:answer/id #uuid "4822c638-df09-5a29-b181-ed51e650cdfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411716} {:answer/id #uuid "debe288e-f7cd-5ceb-8f13-e4258cc3d96c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411803} {:answer/id #uuid "e02c333f-cc9c-5916-848d-431524aca433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411804}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411715} :answer-field/id #uuid "a596b6c7-9c32-5ca9-bbc7-7ea06ecbb649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dd343afe-c54e-593d-8dc2-ed57fc5e3a91" :question/math-academy-id "q-143625" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =P(X<\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ba7b9e6-076b-57c8-a49f-c2f233d245f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413642}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413642} :answer-field/id #uuid "0665a259-196d-5f49-8d9f-3fe90bc699e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88b74bce-a0de-5462-a031-109e23f8056b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413652}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413652} :answer-field/id #uuid "477031a5-7b05-568a-bf03-26feccc03a5b" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413674} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbd845b6-8d50-552b-a3b4-be72d5608d5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413671}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413671} :answer-field/id #uuid "85b347a0-a9d6-50d2-b46b-77ca83ad92a9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c6da89-1bf9-5c09-a900-2173a27faf06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413638}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413638} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb56abab-e923-5821-a5e5-dad20e12f612" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c65cad00-e92b-5864-82b7-3093ffea2302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413661}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413661} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8f099d4-13c7-5012-be7b-31df44a55312" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "774de0b5-5c02-58cd-a5ae-6ac59d12337a" :question/math-academy-id "q-213114" :question/problem "Consider the set $B=\\{2,4,6\\}$ and the relation $R=\\{(x,y)\\in {B}^{2}\\,:\\,x∣y\\}.$\nFill in the missing values in the adjacency matrix of the relation:\n\n|  | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| $4$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $0$ |\n| $6$ | {{field-4}} | $0$ | {{field-5}} |" :question/worked-solution "If a relation $R$ is defined over $A=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},…,{a}_{m}\\}$ and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},…{b}_{n}\\}$ of cardinalities $m$ and $n,$ respectively, the *adjacency matrix* of $R$ is a $m\\times n$-matrix (table), where the element ${r}_{ij}$ at the intersection of the $i$th row and the $j$th column is given by\n\n$$\n{r}_{ij}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,\\text{if }{a}_{i}\\,R\\,{b}_{j}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe relation $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {B}^{2}$ with $x∣y.$\n\nLet's consider each row in our table.\n\n- If $x=2,$ then the values $y=2,4,6$ satisfy $x∣y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(2,2),$ $(2,4),$ and $(2,6),$ and we write $1$ in the intersection of the $1$st row and the $1$st column, in the intersection of the $1$st row and the $2$nd column, and in the intersection of the $1$st row and the $3$rd column in the adjacency matrix.\n\n- If $x=4,$ then the value $y=4$ satisfies $x∣y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(4,4),$ and we write $1$ in the intersection of the $2$nd row and the $2$nd column in the adjacency matrix.\n\n- If $x=6,$ then the value $y=6$ satisfies $x∣y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(6,6),$ and we write $1$ in the intersection of the $3$rd row and the $3$rd column in the adjacency matrix.\n\nAll the other cells in the matrix must be filled with zeros. Therefore, we have the following adjacency matrix:\n\n|  | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $4$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $6$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413694 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a19bac-653a-5eee-9c2f-41a4b7bbc01e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472874} {:answer/id #uuid "2f193e35-b8be-5ea4-bf86-0a381a9f2e69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472875}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472875} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad5dfd31-b4df-5ee3-a703-03f13f39eb84" :answer-field/key "$(✠,♣)$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b808580-7a64-5663-b6ca-9281d1ff47e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472876} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa6bc08-886b-529d-9d06-e2bde7d8ac56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472877}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472876} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dbacaa8-ff71-5012-8acb-759fa0f15267" :answer-field/key "$(♣,♠)$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa3885af-7f7c-5d34-a944-d8f36b8f0d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472878} {:answer/id #uuid "be577392-cb10-5612-af5e-b71a08d83712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472879}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472878} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2c19d87-12f9-58f4-a383-06319f467bdd" :answer-field/key "$(♠,✠)$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "93d6ac86-9246-53ae-8020-58de7dcc7070" :question/math-academy-id "q-213094" :question/problem "|  | $✠$ | $♣$ | $♠$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $✠$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $♣$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $♠$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nThe adjacency matrix of the relation $R,$ defined on the set $\\{✠,♣,♠\\},$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a relation $R$ is defined over $A=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},…,{a}_{m}\\}$ and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},…{b}_{n}\\}$ of cardinalities $m$ and $n,$ respectively, the *adjacency matrix* of $R$ is a $m\\times n$-matrix (or table), where the element ${r}_{ij}$ at the intersection of the $i$th row and the $j$th column is given by\n\n$$\n{r}_{ij}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,\\text{if }{a}_{i}\\,R\\,{b}_{j}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(✠,♣)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the adjacency matrix has $1$ on the intersection of the $✠$-row and the $♣$-column.\n\n- The pair $(♣,♠)$ does not belong to the relation since the adjacency matrix has $0$ on the intersection of the $♣$-row and the $♠$-column.\n\n- The pair $(♠,✠)$ does not belong to the relation since the adjacency matrix has $0$ on the intersection of the $♠$-row and the $✠$-column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(✠,♣)$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf4df8e9-1089-52a8-8fc4-5cb8c93337a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413659}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413659} :answer-field/id #uuid "5596bbe9-cd58-5494-884b-6a7498912540" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb5492ab-8752-5496-97c7-a39039240230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413658}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413658} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce07eb8-fd06-5401-9545-1a8f1505f812" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413677} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bff79e1-4d90-5045-88dc-0027149e07b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413647}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413647} :answer-field/id #uuid "8503c08c-ce71-5a1b-89fb-500b8cd7dd52" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413678} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95001e8b-9839-5f72-8653-a0fbf0785b05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413655}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413655} :answer-field/id #uuid "a35bec16-de5c-5350-a43b-cc13f8592078" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d8c9da-fa6b-57b8-ac61-ead9f12c077b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413651}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413651} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4120405-0f3e-5edc-a2e6-881c9a53b97c" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80ebed47-2563-51af-aaa3-ffac89b613bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413650}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413650} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7433bc2-749d-5ea5-a463-f66c626a5580" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cff8e13-d990-55d5-bfc3-2b19181defd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413653}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413653} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9f54a7f-d74c-52b0-87da-05b966c210d9" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a9e513d0-e8df-5b01-bf4e-b611860d77a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-213121" :question/problem "Consider the sets $A=\\{1,4,8\\}$ and $B=\\{0,6,12\\},$ and the relation $R=\\{(x,y)\\in A\\times B\\,:\\,x∣y\\}.$\nFill in the missing values in the adjacency matrix of the relation:\n\n|  | $0$ | $6$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| $4$ | {{field-4}} | $0$ | {{field-5}} |\n| $8$ | {{field-6}} | {{field-7}} | $0$ |" :question/worked-solution "If a relation $R$ is defined over $A=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},…,{a}_{m}\\}$ and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},…{b}_{n}\\}$ of cardinalities $m$ and $n,$ respectively, the *adjacency matrix* of $R$ is a $m\\times n$-matrix (table), where the element ${r}_{ij}$ at the intersection of the $i$th row and the $j$th column is given by\n\n$$\n{r}_{ij}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,\\text{if }{a}_{i}\\,R\\,{b}_{j}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe relation $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in A\\times B$ with $x∣y.$\n\nLet's consider each row in our table.\n\n- If $x=1,$ then the values $y=0,6,12$ satisfy $x∣y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(1,0),$ $(1,6),$ and $(1,12),$ and we write $1$ in the intersection of the $1$st row and the $1$st column, in the intersection of the $1$st row and the $2$nd column, and in the intersection of the $1$st row and the $3$rd column in the adjacency matrix.\n\n- If $x=4,$ then the values $y=0,12$ satisfy $x∣y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(4,0)$ and $(4,12),$ and we write $1$ in the intersection of the $2$nd row and the $1$st column and in the intersection of the $2$nd row and the $3$rd column in the adjacency matrix.\n\n- If $x=8,$ then the value $y=0$ satisfies $x∣y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(8,0),$ and we write $1$ in the intersection of the $3$rd row and the $1$st column in the adjacency matrix.\n\nAll the other cells in the matrix must be filled with zeros. Therefore, we have the following adjacency matrix:\n\n|  | $0$ | $6$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $8$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16b0e90e-a9a2-53c3-a98d-d5ff68d7b96c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472880} {:answer/id #uuid "e45cb6db-8c29-536d-b9cd-b8ae5e6b7b97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472881}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472880} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee29d82-6e2b-5277-8ec9-1f72315bd17f" :answer-field/key "$(4,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473835} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e71f3623-7599-5c55-96f6-313885cc01a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472882} {:answer/id #uuid "8fbaa2d1-3c66-526e-a54d-05444b706c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472883}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472883} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c5eea00-e7de-5d4e-bc9d-dc27601cc6d9" :answer-field/key "$(8,6)$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2ba602-990d-52ac-8b25-1263667dcc65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472884} {:answer/id #uuid "457cc2fe-dfd8-5b88-b883-eebdc274a68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472885}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472885} :answer-field/id #uuid "58f7ebd0-f7ec-51b3-8e24-dffd8a1498c6" :answer-field/key "$(2,3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e24d1221-5380-50fb-b4e2-6e139d57675a" :question/math-academy-id "q-213100" :question/problem "|  | $3$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $8$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nThe adjacency matrix of the relation $R,$ defined over the sets $\\{2,4,8\\}$ and $\\{3,6\\},$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a relation $R$ is defined over $A=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},…,{a}_{m}\\}$ and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},…{b}_{n}\\}$ of cardinalities $m$ and $n,$ respectively, the *adjacency matrix* of $R$ is a $m\\times n$-matrix (or table), where the element ${r}_{ij}$ at the intersection of the $i$th row and the $j$th column is given by\n\n$$\n{r}_{ij}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,\\text{if }{a}_{i}\\,R\\,{b}_{j}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(4,3)$ does not belong to the relation since the adjacency matrix has $0$ on the intersection of the $4$-row and the $3$-column.\n\n- The pair $(8,6)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the adjacency matrix has $1$ on the intersection of the $8$-row and the $6$-column.\n\n- The pair $(2,3)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the adjacency matrix has $1$ on the intersection of the $2$-row and the $3$-column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(8,6)$; $(2,3)$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419853 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "384b21df-8a7c-5b30-9125-1330da362a5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419836} {:answer/id #uuid "3e21377a-680e-57d6-80e2-410c96b326e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419837} {:answer/id #uuid "6c20cdc4-8968-5346-8c22-76a6ecf55625" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419839} {:answer/id #uuid "e2afce84-edf6-5026-8a56-a45c4ffb8701" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419843} {:answer/id #uuid "f1943a76-0ce9-5efd-8b74-da642c9f9e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419845}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419839} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0b9338f-ce76-54a7-9f1b-a16c716aaa54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a05ac3ca-da7d-5bdc-b9ed-2ee65cee279b" :question/math-academy-id "q-158421" :question/problem "Compute $P(-1<X<0)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12}({x}^{2}+2),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{8} & 1<x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1<X<0) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{12}({x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+2x]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}([\\frac{1}{3}(0)^{3}+2(0)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}+2(-1)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(0+\\frac{1}{3}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419955 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9092706e-4579-52cd-b336-558d7e1b9f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419896} {:answer/id #uuid "b909905a-559d-5031-bfb7-8668badafec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}(x+3)}{324}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424137}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424137} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbd2268b-230b-5334-ac68-b3b22356482f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "dad3449e-8974-53d7-9ad6-1544954b39d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-210788" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{108}x(x+2),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $0\\le x\\le 6,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{108}t(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{324}{t}^{2}(t+3)|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{3}}{324}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{108}, & 0\\le x\\le 6 \\\\ 1, & x>6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15bb385e-7f13-50d3-937e-b59ebadbf90b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9e^{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420173}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420173} :answer-field/id #uuid "49fca85c-c10d-570a-9fbd-829efc317583" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "75e9cee8-821a-5456-9b71-a9061b7a8387" :question/math-academy-id "q-341252" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}}$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **even** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ What is the value of $f(-3)?$\n\n$f(-3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ the even extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,\\pi ), \\\\ F(-x), & x\\in (-\\pi ,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =F(-x) \\\\  & =(-x)^{2}{e}^{(-x)^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =(-3)^{2}{e}^{(-3)^{2}}=9{e}^{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03fbd85f-b443-5e0c-9c2a-949a37212341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/45/4544c4662d43872a4b36bdb0fec343de92ae60a9357d952c4c1d4683c6dc5e2b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420386} {:answer/id #uuid "065f51d0-87f5-5d0a-beff-e1ffeb43d4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/43/430e795e30015f0cad5add0db6360890dadca7b2829947aeb5d40999a08be201.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420387} {:answer/id #uuid "133bd8dc-2c5b-5e1b-bfb2-e4928c76cb5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/42/428dbace9da052a9a308996f661f17249c72798f72d7aff416e82e2a747860ba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420388} {:answer/id #uuid "68af38a9-4172-580e-b666-d3cbc1377bf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/41/41937d29a553f82e3f40c698773ab7f87c7743c16c6ee74fe23ed4edd74fe226.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420390} {:answer/id #uuid "fe62726e-5545-5152-8439-a9f4dd17bb4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/71/7188822007990d41967c09a32f58911494a2c0e2e48a30d1461d398f95178377.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420395}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420388} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c4bea35-db14-526a-a533-f1c203bb2ae0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1bca56bb-980a-59df-8356-0638316b5266" :question/math-academy-id "q-174367" :question/problem "Which of the following is the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of the subset $A=\\{m,r,t\\}$ of $X=\\{m,n,r,s,t\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set $\\{m,r,t\\}$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/1f/1fd2100d57c3483e737dc40298d4d5f61099ebc2863c54839906b66183acf576.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $m,r$ and $t$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5876baf4-837d-5703-a553-2a933946b7af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/3068b57e654d320836833f2e8852a0e1fbffd8d35e9825f9152082e8f4824f3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420389} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec41f8d-3b1b-5812-9900-158cda061db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/28a91b86412c4aee3e560ab931cece60b018d5f6cb7bfc58a5708397a5115e66.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420391} {:answer/id #uuid "8af772ff-67fa-5e4c-8c75-dfb82ea441bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d7/d77304e3deb98dc692121763451260c7e4009cff1c22aa8a05a7735fef032c45.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420392} {:answer/id #uuid "9931fd7f-38ac-5c61-8d34-f2a0e53f7a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/322e21c2df0269a54bec0dce99fa46ab637bad8951ea76339a15fad4243355c9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420393} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a601e7-f054-57e4-9e05-e9374871dc43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/23/238769d3933fbdeaf383e2bd34393c89af4e9aeecd95452d33f166ad115e0c2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420394}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420389} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf8ea8f5-c032-5e49-884a-cc5191da30a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "29b59535-24cf-5f4f-a890-c8446f20f105" :question/math-academy-id "q-174368" :question/problem "Which of the following is the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of the subset $A=\\{2,4,8\\}$ of $X=\\{0,2,4,6,8\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set $\\{2,4,8\\}$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/85/850019897d92b0a8d3340c091cee15342be20e99e7578a9fca23f88804e3bf28.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $2,4$ and $8$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06a255f8-64ef-51d8-a6e6-a071190bf006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423059} {:answer/id #uuid "23d2d105-cdbc-500b-881f-d9e0d158fa84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423061} {:answer/id #uuid "28421387-3618-5282-a14b-84e4566ab27b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423062} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc57884-296c-5280-8d50-e3fcc9ff86ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423075} {:answer/id #uuid "fc72619e-93b0-55af-ae1f-db797a4bfb4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423076}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423076} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac73eb15-075e-5981-aef0-815786fcaa0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3576b4c9-6bad-5c07-bd64-6e08d7444e14" :question/math-academy-id "q-126021" :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\le -4)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\le -1, \\\\ 0,\\, & x>-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -4) & =P(-\\infty <X\\le -4) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-4}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}]}_{-\\infty }^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a01ed84-7ed4-5f6f-a73e-9bd30af3fabb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423065} {:answer/id #uuid "7acfc4ce-813f-5b26-908f-36ee952d848e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423069} {:answer/id #uuid "81adb032-9089-5587-9426-36f061380efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423071} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe28e04-3646-5d84-8159-6ca62c717e0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423073} {:answer/id #uuid "d012b452-3404-5413-b1e0-608d83d5420b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423074}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423065} :answer-field/id #uuid "aad6b045-a52a-569f-a198-e336ad216b28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5cfff2a4-1c49-516b-a57f-2fc4f75675f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126017" :question/problem "Compute $P(X>6)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =P(6<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{6}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423083 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "395effed-4bfa-582d-b3e2-bbe356c7243d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453472} {:answer/id #uuid "621726bd-f7b9-5d1c-90ed-dd4a419d69d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453473}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453473} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb064ed9-57d4-5777-8d35-09cf4b57705a" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "358ddacc-d123-58d8-925f-e9a4f0f35a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453474} {:answer/id #uuid "baf4e056-a6c9-5afa-bdb9-542a77805b71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453475}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453474} :answer-field/id #uuid "a978a13e-4c20-5a6d-b91d-7b677821d028" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454487} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "227ac4ed-ec8b-55fd-a18c-e213264735bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453476} {:answer/id #uuid "6e59a1d7-c74a-566f-a558-8b5ff6c8e1c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453477}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453476} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2e03518-33b3-5350-9a82-0e219b6dab78" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5d743af0-a7a6-59cf-8a8b-38734a18e7f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-160458" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3x-1},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\le 0,$ we have $f(x)=3{e}^{3x-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\n$$ is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{e}^{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x-1}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}-0 \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is false. Since statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\n$$ is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423084 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba238c0a-584c-5ae7-a738-fc7794fd15bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453460} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4ad8a0-ddad-591e-ada0-ddaf6c95f293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453461}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453461} :answer-field/id #uuid "a40ef891-cc3c-51db-885c-7ec524281ffa" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454480} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5f06e7f-7080-514c-b311-eef93e6db768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453462} {:answer/id #uuid "e37290c2-bc90-585f-bb57-e06daa169737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453463}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453463} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1678b1-1651-57aa-9ede-da2c2ed4ec4f" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454481} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74a4e92c-9f38-5f08-b27c-b20a2daf8744" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453464} {:answer/id #uuid "f92c823f-dd97-5983-95bf-0ef1693de5d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453465}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453465} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b23395f-4642-5914-969e-ff7e32133f85" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7af6cdaa-d1ff-562c-9d47-7e9a37adf5ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-160446" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)={e}^{-x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\n$$ is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is true. Since statements “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$” and $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\n$$ are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$”; $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1;\n$$ “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "186b12e8-0537-5623-ab6f-d5dfb2e0cdcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423196}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423196} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce23bf5e-8b29-5cf7-9b38-cc60d7fad1c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fc8861f3-8c91-59c6-b70f-78e5364379e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-341817" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2, & x\\in [0,\\pi ) \\\\ 3, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{4}.$\n\n${a}_{4}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi .$ Also, $f(x)=-2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi )$ and $f(x)=3$ for $x\\in [-\\pi ,0).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}_{-\\pi }^{0}-\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423942 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "947b312e-ee99-59a7-af09-a903fd2e1d0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423919} {:answer/id #uuid "abcc5b71-338b-577c-85eb-afb6840553f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423923} {:answer/id #uuid "ad0f1713-2b05-514d-a10e-779d012891f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423924} {:answer/id #uuid "b948344f-4402-5976-9213-69a3217d38b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423926} {:answer/id #uuid "f8739b76-a0ab-5c98-9470-0410c9781bfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423935}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423926} :answer-field/id #uuid "df10270c-afeb-5cba-9cb6-73907dc215c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0437d140-6528-59da-a359-aaf4bce3a4ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-164160" :question/problem "Given $X∼U\\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\},$ compute $P(X<2).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\},$ and the set $S=\\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}$ has $|S|=6$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}, & x=0,1,2,3,4,5 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $2$ items $(0,1)$ that satisfy $X<2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X<2)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42bd1876-65cb-5fd8-a63d-6a5b4ed622b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423910} {:answer/id #uuid "647f830c-4930-5419-a92d-35fb9d117c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423912} {:answer/id #uuid "65710dca-584a-5538-8392-0c75db50947c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423913} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3ca409-a4c3-54ba-b34a-0eaab0215bcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423921} {:answer/id #uuid "d00c4e38-efbb-57f3-bf1e-8cd2dd37778d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423930}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423921} :answer-field/id #uuid "17dd14c1-f0a6-5f73-9ff5-1250112c1e2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3fa88aaf-70b9-5b39-b375-a1ff9fc14a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96778" :question/problem "Given that $X∼U\\{3,7,9,10\\},$ compute $P(X=9).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{3,7,9,10\\},$ and the set $S=\\{3,7,9,10\\}$ has $|S|=4$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & x=3,7,9,10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=9)=f(9)=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26cab201-dd5a-5522-a7c5-25241811d134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423908} {:answer/id #uuid "5b6c4c06-c4a6-59a0-90bc-5dba036d765a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423911} {:answer/id #uuid "771bbc36-1481-5967-acf3-99e3381b2049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423915} {:answer/id #uuid "867fb739-bcef-5db1-ad21-be3d3d6e70e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423917} {:answer/id #uuid "e4aa368d-d1cf-529c-b6c7-9e7448c03be7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423934}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423917} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac586fbc-baee-5b6b-94a9-3c6e6210f9e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "49e5ad2d-03f1-55be-ada8-dbc0284264c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-96810" :question/problem "Given $X∼U\\{9,10,11,…,17\\},$ compute $P(X<12).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{9,10,11,…,17\\},$ and the set $S=\\{9,10,11,…,17\\}$ has $|S|=17-9+1=9$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}, & x=9,10,11,…,17 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $X<12$ are $9,10,11.$ There are $3$ of these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X<12)=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a450533-8c93-5f65-b086-433237dedd04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423906} {:answer/id #uuid "16d2517e-9185-5017-857d-9ebe5b8407f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423907} {:answer/id #uuid "35e889ba-9472-5ac8-a25c-ed6d2ba99992" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423909} {:answer/id #uuid "9c17240f-6dc3-5a02-ad81-bc045176e81b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423922} {:answer/id #uuid "de19a84f-848b-52ac-9d4f-56ab8e8d674a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423932}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423922} :answer-field/id #uuid "6928beb7-6d1c-5fe0-9c89-497534fd649e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a7e41369-c44a-5b84-b7fc-e764205aba15" :question/math-academy-id "q-96839" :question/problem "Given $X∼U\\{1,2,3,…,17\\},$ compute $P(2\\le X<9).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{1,2,3,…,17\\},$ and the set $S=\\{1,2,3,…,17\\}$ has $|S|=17-1+1=17$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{17}, & x=1,2,3,…,17 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $7$ items $(2,3,4,5,6,7,8)$ that satisfy $2\\le X<9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(2\\le X<9)=7\\cdot \\frac{1}{17}=\\frac{7}{17}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bf42ba7-f2a3-55cc-af79-9f295ed44f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423916} {:answer/id #uuid "8959248e-670f-5708-9f80-641e8f900f4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423918} {:answer/id #uuid "9875fe05-05a7-53d3-ada2-9e8fce9c093c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423920} {:answer/id #uuid "bf21e23b-1364-514e-b8af-73c89ab25898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423928} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6aedae-2775-57fe-a720-4bb794b417b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423929}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423928} :answer-field/id #uuid "562db703-36ec-5628-89c0-8362fc1a8c9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b4439689-3a8b-5ab4-811b-957340569ef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-96838" :question/problem "Given $X∼U\\{11,13,14,16,20\\},$ compute $P(13\\le X<16).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{11,13,14,16,20\\},$ and the set $S=\\{11,13,14,16,20\\}$ has $|S|=5$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}, & x=11,13,14,16,20 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $2$ items $(13,14)$ that satisfies $13\\le X<16.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(13\\le X<16)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423947 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a09e155-68e9-5775-88e9-0c0dd6011287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423914} {:answer/id #uuid "af474fa2-5b82-5e5b-919d-49bf9a3d89c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423925} {:answer/id #uuid "be11ebe4-c5f0-5452-93cf-c1171aabffec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423927} {:answer/id #uuid "d0318c22-f087-5f8c-bdd5-bca3ec896998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423931} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a79c61-b7dd-5a80-b81d-55f14b24abc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423933}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423914} :answer-field/id #uuid "f32b7f4b-707c-5946-80d1-f757bb8e4cf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c83e57db-b20b-5f69-af71-6e6e6a8e413f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96780" :question/problem "Given that $X∼U\\{13,14,18\\},$ compute $P(X=14).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{13,14,18\\},$ and the set $S=\\{13,14,18\\}$ has $|S|=3$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & x=13,14,18 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=14)=f(14)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1745b6-630b-529f-9136-c40f62c94d25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2231" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423968} {:answer/id #uuid "3f517b2d-d281-5139-846d-3d24808ad7b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0821" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423972} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7853be-90ec-5040-a947-22a3b32a3ad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6065" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423980} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0cfc25-ccc8-5d6f-a075-ad935990a0fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1353" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423988} {:answer/id #uuid "e72eff5e-65c2-554e-894e-cea3af368c6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8647" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423991}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423988} :answer-field/id #uuid "06adbee9-5f6f-500e-9c80-babe38453b76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0be3a602-67d5-5cf7-8f80-aff71640198e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96406" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(1),$ calculate $P(X\\ge 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(1).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X\\ge 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}{|}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a753c6c-3899-5081-81c1-9c51956a63b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423967} {:answer/id #uuid "39d93c58-7d48-5de8-9930-8560bb4ab222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5932" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423970} {:answer/id #uuid "b5df255f-d5f8-5d26-a865-2d00936b6ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6585" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423986} {:answer/id #uuid "e0577aef-a54a-5b56-9e1d-4dcfbccf5fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5276" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423989} {:answer/id #uuid "f293deb7-7ba9-56a2-ae3f-b82352272b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6187" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423993}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423989} :answer-field/id #uuid "c78b8e7b-777c-5193-bc20-a17bf3a58b7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "24af5ca9-8d38-530b-8002-d4db8feaa5d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96345" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right),$ calculate $P(X<1).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-3x/4}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<1)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-3x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3x/4}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3/4}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.5276\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a50814-795d-5d28-8e92-209754c2af10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3654" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423965} {:answer/id #uuid "20637901-6ccf-5b0b-8845-93cfcc926093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3611" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423966} {:answer/id #uuid "4d1edc2d-b633-52ba-85a7-13aec31489a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1286" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423973} {:answer/id #uuid "6fadb770-777f-5d25-8c8e-520eb1a7bac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1329" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423977} {:answer/id #uuid "78e06ba4-70f9-51bf-9980-6444eb5316e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1358" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423979}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423977} :answer-field/id #uuid "64885566-dbce-53b8-b813-e5b5f9f5627a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "548f5527-3c2c-5249-846d-012dddb74912" :question/math-academy-id "q-96417" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(1\\le X\\le 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(1\\le X\\le 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-6}+{e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1329\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424004 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b8a2e77-056b-5c7d-a4a5-f0b85875f98a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0498" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423971} {:answer/id #uuid "4e91c1c2-03b1-5f7b-accf-22d6915d4b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2865" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423974} {:answer/id #uuid "95ffeb01-adda-57d6-881e-fcb39a8b7a3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0067" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423982} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef5aef2-1def-50a9-8422-76dce776ddf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0025" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423983} {:answer/id #uuid "f083723d-90d7-5c3f-8b0b-f6cf96ee2b97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3679" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423992}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423983} :answer-field/id #uuid "0782fde0-7971-5f6d-aba6-4b1f607a9ca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9e3c60ce-47c9-5c4f-b8dd-973c8222fab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-96407" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $U∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(U\\ge 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $U$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nU∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(U\\ge 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U\\ge 3) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-2u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2u}{|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-6} \\\\  & ≈0.0025\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e3d93ec-eb09-56cb-a416-5e2e7bec5a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424020} {:answer/id #uuid "19f85468-debe-56c4-9c7b-72ce62714596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424024} {:answer/id #uuid "4538c02d-cc56-5357-9692-c45dbd1ff415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424033} {:answer/id #uuid "b411a94b-c858-532e-8504-f3fa46b1d90a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424040} {:answer/id #uuid "eb1915dd-5764-5752-856c-c61ccdaa99f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424041}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424020} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e81c82-0d29-5aa1-9b44-d0a62600de34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2b0137dd-0ad1-53cf-acd8-0bbd632c8d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-96334" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,1],$ compute $P(-2\\le X\\le 2).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,1],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & -3\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2\\le X\\le 2) & =P(-2\\le X\\le 1) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "160a5126-2e24-5c1b-be6a-a06e49dea788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424022} {:answer/id #uuid "2e30620f-4add-5a5d-8a10-63fa89353160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424028} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1ef539-7e09-5084-96af-05c9d696698e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424030} {:answer/id #uuid "8df8f671-8474-59ab-86d4-5301bd912c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424037} {:answer/id #uuid "a32c4229-ee76-5056-a461-20d9ac56ae28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424038}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424030} :answer-field/id #uuid "99010428-33fd-5dd7-a898-3d5893398292" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6a51ea05-5e14-5ec8-80f9-413f5ec71214" :question/math-academy-id "q-130692" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,4],$ compute $P(W\\ge 1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,4],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & 0\\le w\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\ge 1) & =P(1\\le W\\le 4) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424052 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1acc037d-bce5-53b6-8323-1b252862f034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424025} {:answer/id #uuid "83a78c2b-ec57-5782-818b-1ebb0a0fb0c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424036} {:answer/id #uuid "af55ac66-d6ee-5c68-93d5-ab774affd010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424039} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a1a7df-15e9-518c-9fce-7ec892fe2232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424042} {:answer/id #uuid "f8195f95-abed-5f7b-abf8-51d99c4e7df0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424043}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424043} :answer-field/id #uuid "efac0da0-aee9-5e9c-ae73-a7e2c584348e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b864ebe6-e085-5252-a91f-4ca0cb314e2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96284" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ compute $P(U<-3).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $U$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le u\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20},\\, & -10\\le u\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U<-3) & =P(-10\\le U<-3) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-10}^{-3}f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-10}^{-3}\\frac{1}{20}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-(-10)}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424053 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e99867f-cfc9-54c7-b348-5f78d1c3d9fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424026} {:answer/id #uuid "25c1f749-943c-58ad-b0b0-8e9b295a57ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424027} {:answer/id #uuid "3f72b617-3a2d-566c-9b4c-88d79b0fb5b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424031} {:answer/id #uuid "3feeccff-adf9-5ba7-9142-c8b271570281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424032} {:answer/id #uuid "fe28eeec-5654-567a-b9a6-2676f4eb678e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424044}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424031} :answer-field/id #uuid "d020dc5f-a9e6-5b1f-9ba1-79c84664ccd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b9258154-36aa-5bfe-9428-732732589876" :question/math-academy-id "q-96279" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ compute $P(W\\le 5).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7},\\, & 3\\le w\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\le 5) & =P(3\\le W\\le 5) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{5-3}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424054 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "107d2581-115e-5fcf-a7ba-4b8a4e067792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424021} {:answer/id #uuid "19b9c547-b3de-5a3b-af9a-1d4bd21add26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424023} {:answer/id #uuid "33ea49c6-ab8b-5f20-989d-636291cc3105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424029} {:answer/id #uuid "51df5392-9584-5939-887e-e5eb023f5973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424034} {:answer/id #uuid "534fce73-0f67-5e15-aa99-7cc2da173c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424035}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424023} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9e477c-a83d-55bd-a460-7bef9eab339b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f0228a94-8a4a-532e-880c-3c74fb2a7fa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-96333" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ compute $P(0\\le X\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\pi },\\, & -\\pi \\le x\\le \\pi , \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-0)}{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424085 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e7252d1-7bec-51e8-895b-5c303264ccf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424055} {:answer/id #uuid "13c231a4-02c9-519e-a16e-fac887b7ebc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424056} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf10b9f-0537-5d79-9473-d19b73e91528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424071} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e07a66-e2fe-5302-a36e-006523c84d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424072} {:answer/id #uuid "b60edc09-3248-59be-ad60-c9699fb3762c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424073}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424073} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee00c64-0bcc-5caf-9fda-20fec973369a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0312f13e-9d46-503a-8af4-69a3bd5d2f16" :question/math-academy-id "q-130870" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{x}, & -\\sqrt{e}<x<-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & -1\\le x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x{|}_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}+{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{e}+\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{e}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33e3d064-30ad-5eab-99b7-4055df83c43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424059} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab28cb4-c411-518a-b8f9-3b843cb43bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e-1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424066} {:answer/id #uuid "828c703f-f7c1-5221-a107-3b628a52c6ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e+1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424067} {:answer/id #uuid "c327ff22-8621-594a-a52d-99bb4e2941b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424074} {:answer/id #uuid "de4f8756-22a2-5a93-8cf4-1f6ce720de08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424074} :answer-field/id #uuid "c45ae753-611c-5337-a1ef-57b485b3183d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "713f9e9d-4bae-5fb8-b6da-37cc8d4aaf0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130872" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x}{5}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5x}, & 1\\le x<e\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{6x}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{2}{5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{5}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{5}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{2x}{5}|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{2e}{5}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea5a4d8-cee6-5f5b-9559-0597059ae4e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424119} {:answer/id #uuid "47fbec0e-7c87-50b2-b20a-31977a9c56d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424122} {:answer/id #uuid "624998d8-03eb-57ee-930b-8fdefbbf7c6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3-{x}^{2}+4x}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424126} {:answer/id #uuid "8370b066-0576-542b-8883-25e20f54d4ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424132} {:answer/id #uuid "8deef2d1-1973-51e5-9cbf-ea501d5e8c27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+12x-9}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424133}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424119} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e5a55d3-f519-5435-8ffd-ee8305a73bcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4087990a-4ed6-57e2-a3df-7711bffc8cc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-89659" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}(x-2),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<3 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $3\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ {\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{x}\\frac{2}{3}(t-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={\\frac{1}{3}t(t-4)|}_{3}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}x(x-4)+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<3 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-4x+3}{3}, & 3\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4d86307-444b-5404-bf96-e83b782452e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424136}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424136} :answer-field/id #uuid "064b270e-fcf7-5b15-ad01-0cc140059469" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "481bd08b-bf47-54b5-b36c-cbccf6d7d5b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-210757" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 1,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={-\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}+1 \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a08189-b91b-5a20-b7ab-cd5b33daebf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/20}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424121} {:answer/id #uuid "63f468a1-66c1-59cb-86ef-0e77953938a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{e}^{-x/20}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424127} {:answer/id #uuid "713d0b3e-c9bb-554a-b337-a9f036666fa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-20{e}^{-x/20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424129} {:answer/id #uuid "74a5f07c-c3bf-5c2c-a586-05b1a17ea2f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-x/20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424130} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1adf91-dd13-599a-aacf-34ab3e99b819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-x/20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424135}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424135} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d1d5c23-5aca-5a94-9f2b-7f2199c25b68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9bc932a7-b704-59fd-b0c1-c79e29ca1ef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-126151" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-x/20},\\, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $x\\ge 0,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{20}{e}^{-t/20}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & =-{e}^{-t/20}{|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/20}+1 \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-x/20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ 1-{e}^{-x/20}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e656111-b56c-58e0-b523-b0edd9650549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424123} {:answer/id #uuid "616c4e05-5002-58ab-b3bb-58e10d3a8092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424125} {:answer/id #uuid "6f86bba4-cf32-5b63-95b2-322fa3b1a857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424128} {:answer/id #uuid "7b06527d-a247-549f-874c-21500db45064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424131} {:answer/id #uuid "99eb6595-a15f-5755-a0e3-76f958a96458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424134}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424128} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e83422-0d19-5c35-89b8-d714903a72c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a285feed-066b-52a2-a5c2-8c1c741cc3d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-89738" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ 1-{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$" :question/worked-solution "We can perform this computation using the complement, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-(1-{e}^{-4}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f9e3f9-5178-5f25-af6a-daa6ab351cf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424116} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbef09a-e8ff-5508-9488-c6c964ed4029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424117} {:answer/id #uuid "17a75073-455d-5976-ba1c-b3f22347a040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424118} {:answer/id #uuid "3111cc62-9d7f-5a21-8f89-33bb0b009b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{48}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424120} {:answer/id #uuid "529bbff1-ee9c-5239-b9f3-b7e4f26f33fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424124}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424117} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8a9fa39-360a-5d80-8fca-fb43fa89be61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cbafb4bb-6bd6-540c-9367-06ab0b677b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-126178" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{96}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}-3), & 1\\le x\\le 3 \\\\ 1, & x>3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>2).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{96}({2}^{4}+2(2)^{2}-3) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{21}{96} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424374 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5547a59d-4082-5471-8b71-d59a07d32d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424339} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0f2fd4-cce9-5b1f-a0fc-bbb4de04e32c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424344} {:answer/id #uuid "b6415cf2-9dee-5ed8-8c70-9e39a6b7b363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424355} {:answer/id #uuid "cf10babe-4fb2-5ed6-b0e3-51c161bbe192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424358} {:answer/id #uuid "f912b078-5c68-5e79-9616-1cc70dfbee36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424365}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424344} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a04253-21f8-57fa-9da2-eb6b04eff7f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1f759cee-8f8e-57dc-b752-40d429fccaa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-97647" :question/problem "A child is playing with a tablet. The apps on the tablet are labeled with numbers $4$ through $21.$ If the child chooses an app at random, what is the probability that the app number they pick is more than $16?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number of the app picked. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{4,5,…,21\\},$ and we wish to compute $P(X>16).$\n\nIn general, if $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{4,5,…,21\\},$ and the set $S=\\{4,5,…,21\\}$ has $|S|=21-4+1=18$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{18}, & x=4,5,…,21 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $X>16$ are $17,18,19,20,21.$ There are $5$ of these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X>16)=5\\cdot \\frac{1}{18}=\\frac{5}{18}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424376 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820ae2a2-894d-5114-98c1-0c069a04fb00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424348} {:answer/id #uuid "90fcb279-3814-5dab-a9da-34cb34cf2297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424351} {:answer/id #uuid "a2517864-8ff2-5d85-b806-1c79fc85fd80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424352} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc11d3d-3403-5323-a459-1449e6d907e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424360} {:answer/id #uuid "e3430a41-06ca-5f20-8875-54682b73bce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424361}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424351} :answer-field/id #uuid "e77545cc-1b3a-5e85-b752-ea1b743f1c43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "574dc243-2e55-5ce7-9e9d-a12e501cd5c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-97660" :question/problem "Jack wants to buy a single issue of a particular comic series with $80$ issues. Unfortunately, the comic store has neither the first $3$ issues nor the final issue in stock. If Jack buys a comic at random from the available issues, what is the probability that he chooses either issue $20$ or issue $23?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the issue Jack selects. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{4,5,…,79\\},$ and we wish to compute $P(X=20\\,\\,or\\,\\,X=23).$\n\nIn general, if $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{4,5,…,79\\},$ and the set $S=\\{4,5,…,79\\}$ has $|S|=79-4+1=76$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{76}, & x=4,5,…,79 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy the given condition are $20,23.$ There are $2$ of these elements. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=20\\,\\,or\\,\\,X=23)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{76}=\\frac{1}{38}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15086c87-9c13-579c-ba6e-748eaf611b0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424334} {:answer/id #uuid "69e75bc6-66fd-55e9-bf42-99525bc872c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424343} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec6426d-a527-5edf-abdc-752ce809d846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424346} {:answer/id #uuid "7bcc0a75-c778-5ff4-bb53-0a28275cff60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424347} {:answer/id #uuid "cf03c069-f7d1-542b-9880-50a243a3e4a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424357}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424343} :answer-field/id #uuid "24d10336-4f92-5c3b-8f87-5930254510c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a490336d-2a2e-5374-a15f-1401e77380a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-148408" :question/problem "When rolling a fair six-sided die, what is the probability of getting a prime number?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number on which the die lands. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{1,2,…,6\\},$ and we wish to compute $P(X\\in \\{2,3,5\\}).$\n\nIn general, if $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{1,2,…,6\\},$ and the set $S=\\{1,2,…,6\\}$ has $|S|=6$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}, & x=1,2,…,6 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $X\\in \\{2,3,5\\}$ are $2,3,5.$ There are $3$ of these elements. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X\\in \\{2,3,5\\})=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e5e3c03-d706-5575-856d-866eb3d9500c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424333} {:answer/id #uuid "3c08f617-d8ee-596f-b133-64ab4350a77c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424335} {:answer/id #uuid "67067611-aa63-5326-8173-b77d14f9f6aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424342} {:answer/id #uuid "dabb82bc-b608-55c9-b787-5af6495f857a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424359} {:answer/id #uuid "fc726ac5-a2c5-55ad-81bd-c76c122c6b10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424366}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424335} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8df995d-74a1-505c-a3a5-e60115444fb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e66fdc5b-c55e-53fe-9d08-47c56ef73570" :question/math-academy-id "q-148406" :question/problem "The only available spaces in a multi-story parking lot are on the second floor, numbered from $215$ to $268.$\nIf Emma parks in one of the spaces at random, what is the probability that she parks in a space which is numbered between $234$ and $245$ inclusive?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the parking space Emma picks. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{215,216,…,268\\},$ and we wish to compute $P(234\\le X\\le 245).$\n\nIn general, if $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{215,216,…,268\\},$ and the set $S=\\{215,216,…,268\\}$ has $|S|=268-215+1=54$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{54}, & x=215,216,…,268 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $234\\le X\\le 245$ are $234,235,…,245.$ There are $245-234+1=12$ of these elements. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(234\\le X\\le 245)=12\\cdot \\frac{1}{54}=\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25462498-9604-5abf-a03e-8496f16cbe50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1353" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424530} {:answer/id #uuid "68d43eaf-e9d2-5c03-90f1-2c5494830081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1435" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424544} {:answer/id #uuid "a0dfb2f8-0b7f-57b3-99b5-9e1f339559e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1553" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424548} {:answer/id #uuid "b69c52c0-8e2e-5c56-a7ce-24a1cf21399a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1155" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424554} {:answer/id #uuid "ec1596e7-46b5-53ff-8622-206707f0ad5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1233" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424562}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424530} :answer-field/id #uuid "30cd8153-4b27-59dd-bd60-d805ce68023b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "04d4be2b-e767-5839-99c5-470d8cac4dc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-132193" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{2}),$ calculate $P(X>\\sqrt{2}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>\\sqrt{2})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>\\sqrt{2}) & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty }\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{2}x}{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15122c8a-6495-57b5-bc9a-8504dc7b9d5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3927" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424528} {:answer/id #uuid "a2cad5b5-d85b-5775-9ae3-23738e9a9e95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3279" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424550} {:answer/id #uuid "adb828a8-83fa-5e72-8b2f-372fd52cbd31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3337" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424551} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb85eac-0073-5d12-9fad-bb5b6c84c2f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3297" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424552} {:answer/id #uuid "b07b0fbc-b758-5397-9f9a-f0c56f381e23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3137" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424553}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424552} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f87a4b8-066c-5da9-b676-ea815d24ff9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "377d9ecb-b1f2-5b7d-b293-34044d6f6558" :question/math-academy-id "q-132173" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right),$ calculate $P(X\\le 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x/5}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X\\le 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{-x/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-x/5}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2/5}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.3297\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fc40c2d-1af0-5adc-a2bc-6557e8adc194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4683" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424533} {:answer/id #uuid "31011ded-b236-51be-8752-9a8a39f1aa2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4836" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424534} {:answer/id #uuid "3a08e9d4-be37-5bcd-b93a-f75705061f0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4886" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424535} {:answer/id #uuid "3e6f8763-9d72-5754-bbed-ce927bc4b0f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4768" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424537} {:answer/id #uuid "47bc7314-1895-551e-8d2a-b165d99e961e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4386" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424540}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424540} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bc8a138-558e-5ca1-bd83-4c4ce4806474" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4b3ef3ac-d2db-5eb8-8c5f-a033b26be69b" :question/math-academy-id "q-132179" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{3}),$ calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{3}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\sqrt{3}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{3})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<\\frac{1}{3}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\sqrt{3}{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}x}{|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\sqrt{3}/3}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.4386\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424577 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44a2b804-976b-516e-8262-d27bd168e200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1155" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424539} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f19cf2-ae03-5a5d-a484-a5c96a8a6ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1328" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424549} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c9e78d-99e5-5ab7-9783-9080b7da6c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1951" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424556} {:answer/id #uuid "e78e8d34-90e2-5ca7-a750-14ec68adc2ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1455" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424561} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ab51fe-7288-559d-9763-4a92ffa3e0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1785" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424563}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424561} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf5a599-01b3-5f07-9129-5e078a5628ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9bd8d602-6713-5d8a-8e29-384c77e10125" :question/math-academy-id "q-96347" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right),$ calculate $P(2<X<3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(2<X<3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/3}{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1}+{e}^{-2/3} \\\\  & ≈0.1455\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424579 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0720396c-abfc-53ff-8ef1-c514b74b2d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1175" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424526} {:answer/id #uuid "2840ed6b-1f83-568f-87c3-170c58ac5221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9592" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424532} {:answer/id #uuid "404222de-38b1-5509-b195-dc8a8808dc04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0489" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424538} {:answer/id #uuid "70d4b207-6b19-5682-92c6-5c0ba818e73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0408" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424545} {:answer/id #uuid "c786b93e-93f4-53da-8bd9-45ac133e7e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424558}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424545} :answer-field/id #uuid "693fb341-39fe-5150-9137-34fee2604c10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "be9c7f67-1bb2-5f32-8555-0a5418fba86d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96412" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(8),$ calculate $P(X>0.4).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(8).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}8{e}^{-8x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X>0.4)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>0.4) & ={\\int }_{0.4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.4}^{\\infty }8{e}^{-8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-8x}{|}_{0.4}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-3.2} \\\\  & ≈0.0408\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424580 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13134444-762f-50b4-bf4c-6865257862e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4411" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424527} {:answer/id #uuid "3b282901-4897-5136-9d46-9253c88fc7f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4885" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424536} {:answer/id #uuid "486ea7b8-8768-5c1b-9819-16e84f6ed54b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4852" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424541} {:answer/id #uuid "8451cd55-2a53-5891-9ae6-f129b4cd4ee2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4799" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424547} {:answer/id #uuid "ded2a796-947a-596a-9be0-948722eda4df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4712" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424559}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424559} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab5409cf-4685-540d-8e56-731571e9e2ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d71bf438-c740-5ac5-956a-edf3ba9d43d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-96421" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(1),$ calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(1).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.5\\le X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}{|}_{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{-0.5} \\\\  & ≈0.4712\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "492f777b-8264-55ab-9be1-d1359bd9513d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424871} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7a5540-6762-5260-9b7f-2a98061bf95e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424872} {:answer/id #uuid "50e4b7f0-64ef-587b-bfde-a4520b836560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424873} {:answer/id #uuid "d60102cb-368c-5209-b3c3-06d9c44b89a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424880} {:answer/id #uuid "ef55c585-a616-50c9-9382-ffb7b5a8ceda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424881}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424881} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce55fccd-c2b9-544b-881d-b59a7e7c0f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2b70eaac-0c45-5da5-8a2f-2002d9071035" :question/math-academy-id "q-89727" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{-|x/3|}}{6},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2},\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d43dadc-2415-595b-83bd-07293e62a4d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424868} {:answer/id #uuid "2d728c61-ee7a-5242-b976-dff68318b24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424870} {:answer/id #uuid "54302da3-4ffd-5ae6-9474-e5f95bb705f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424874} {:answer/id #uuid "86635ef4-b567-5842-a8be-7564b4bc47cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424876} {:answer/id #uuid "c53339f9-decf-5456-b59e-339275bad539" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424879}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424870} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf2e7998-6dc3-5838-ae14-0d427c2b4449" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5d72a8e6-eda0-59be-829b-e0298d5412e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-89695" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{x}, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\le 5).$" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is $F(5)=1-\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{4}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f33f1e-6e04-5ef0-8a18-a9a9635e495a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x+\\frac{11}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424869} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc40166-55c4-53b3-bf06-562cddc8e868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x+\\frac{11}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424875} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0df617-e565-5181-bd27-09321bb7abfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424877} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e9b386-cf97-5734-82c8-f8b9318ea865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424878} {:answer/id #uuid "fbbc1dbf-3cbe-5835-99b1-f9050b0ed224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{27}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}x+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424882}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424875} :answer-field/id #uuid "5340e926-2580-5f2f-bf08-46d25e342346" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "97c91681-ff70-5452-bbfe-e1a92bb2e9d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-126156" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{9}(x-1)(x-4),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $1\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}-\\frac{2}{9}(t-1)(t-4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}-\\frac{2}{9}({t}^{2}-5t+4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{2}{27}{t}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{t}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}t)|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x-(-\\frac{2}{27}+\\frac{5}{9}-\\frac{8}{9}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x+\\frac{11}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x+\\frac{11}{27}, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae0644f-0546-5bc1-aec6-a8d55d6d7d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425359} {:answer/id #uuid "32f46f92-c0b7-5b8c-84c6-59f108c961fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425363} {:answer/id #uuid "65952301-d738-5c6a-b6fc-b85df8529a6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425365} {:answer/id #uuid "c503e550-36c6-5d75-ad74-9d8d0ffca904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425370} {:answer/id #uuid "dea7c8b5-a396-5c8c-a3e3-22fae9de2f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425372}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425372} :answer-field/id #uuid "13b91257-68b8-500a-b201-47daf0478002" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a75bec48-b401-5e54-9492-da413551ed38" :question/math-academy-id "q-130875" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & 1\\le x<2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "201c2488-3b9d-5108-a48b-2c3d64cef328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425362} {:answer/id #uuid "637130b5-f7d6-51c6-b45d-c736d39b3a74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e+3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425364} {:answer/id #uuid "70653d2a-2e94-5850-abe7-6d163b8005a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e-1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425366} {:answer/id #uuid "814d0b3f-29a5-5f01-b16e-f12a0f9ff292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425367} {:answer/id #uuid "f493205a-4bbe-5f60-96f9-afe578c94f3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425373}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425366} :answer-field/id #uuid "b56cdda3-d5c2-5ae0-8fb8-26559a6d5135" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e9404e17-b865-57fd-909a-78dee18906a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130871" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2x}, & 1\\le x<e\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{x}{2}|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{e}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e-1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bdf9085-5e57-5fef-9288-dd2d5b77cfd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425551} {:answer/id #uuid "15b4446a-3837-52de-923e-6861cab63dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425558}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425558} :answer-field/id #uuid "0515496f-04cd-566b-90f7-87a3f4b76092" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425645} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "057eb7f3-190a-5da9-a784-33d6a0e88a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425547} {:answer/id #uuid "c884611a-198a-588d-a475-eb02622d1e56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425621}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425621} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a027e30-e5db-5ef5-823b-5d5213ffe1be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2beb1cb1-5d44-5f64-aa49-099923f8b16b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425568} {:answer/id #uuid "ec2972fd-47e3-5529-9b6d-d5a3d01b3766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425631}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425568} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b781fbf-b13f-5c71-940f-e7a40eb71a60" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c442eea8-eb9b-51fe-9d23-75ab92b8ffe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425618} {:answer/id #uuid "f9060f67-f7b4-5a5d-bfd7-7abf56ccf59e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425636}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425618} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc32ec31-8aab-5e25-95f6-47aed03f7c3b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3df34aa2-66f8-53fb-b84c-e23ff9464f43" :question/math-academy-id "q-342264" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ 3, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | $\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/7a/7afa339233c7e21eda233f5b67ccf8be9e05fb4ce9484c98eaf59eb790e651ab.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}x=-2\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}3=3.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and III are false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/1a/1ac6956ec22cfed2d304cc5c2352cf1fdf4c795ea423e7a19c8e3a3e2dc843ed.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425677 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1124e7b9-2d5f-5e41-894c-4012a241cbb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425553} {:answer/id #uuid "fc0eac61-78a6-5e61-9741-36c63bed5514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425640}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425553} :answer-field/id #uuid "02397001-5967-5501-a894-ba22a52ed078" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425642} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb5b194-82d3-514f-a7ba-8de2203f7d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425588} {:answer/id #uuid "a0bab576-a7aa-5d44-bb81-8dddab1acc90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425609}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425588} :answer-field/id #uuid "43f4ed93-3433-5da6-8034-8da63e770508" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425653} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "134b90c6-da6f-564c-b88c-9cde9a9b37af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425556} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa2deb5-9607-580c-9d2a-b98702d2433d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425600}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425556} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9d9c24a-7b11-59ec-a4a0-6136392a9411" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "930eef55-0159-5954-a696-d7ed742b7ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425605} {:answer/id #uuid "f8fa35e0-047b-50a2-976e-7044fdf2253d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425635}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425605} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c6d28a-a8a0-5b03-a2be-c422eefbc276" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "46096919-32d4-552d-ad62-e0e1723dd83b" :question/math-academy-id "q-342245" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ {x}^{3}, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | $\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/0a/0a29065f008fac7d3fd32d52b2ddc0b7d9360ffd75475f6c169eeb26582d22d2.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}-4x=-4(-2)=8\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}{x}^{3}=(2)^{3}=8.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{true}$ since statements I, II, and III are all true.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/d7/d750ad2f9ea2a85446b94f7b19009ef74eeea25b4ccd1bf8ff4f408a5df381e2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113f0528-6296-5edc-a471-87b1ca2ca4b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425554} {:answer/id #uuid "7686472d-41c3-5025-a423-4ae9721b5993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425597}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425554} :answer-field/id #uuid "08ecb117-6c45-5463-b318-8c285506eabc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425646} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76b55157-f226-54be-8fd3-e576ce7da945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425598} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0e6216-87df-59a6-808e-871e310b9484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425623}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425623} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b521d38-d990-5b0d-80fe-d03ebd685a00" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e34f35d-c327-5601-b6ee-eb5051e0fda7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425561} {:answer/id #uuid "a698678d-21d8-5a48-b894-3c49a5fac693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425612}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425612} :answer-field/id #uuid "60253eb4-3e5a-59a0-8c20-7c861c025f6e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "151f3b2c-1198-5804-bb25-a1fa989b21a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425557} {:answer/id #uuid "64cf008c-66db-51cd-bdbe-6511859f628e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425593}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425557} :answer-field/id #uuid "a102f1e0-40e5-5ef6-a7de-a0e753751c70" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6b957da1-0df2-5626-98d6-1a7c5a3632dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-342601" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{3}+3, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ x+1, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | $\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/2d/2d30d760181c95dd0764b9959ca91febb34e94618bb147d8022dae5745c38a1a.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}((x+2)^{3}+3)=(0)^{3}+3=3\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}(x+1)=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\lim_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement I is false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/fc/fcdf5654322a6deff9d7598590b4e0e1ace6150020b4944ad844976fb0f70230.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425680 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cf9be56-efa9-5355-8976-ae2a23fa9c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425552} {:answer/id #uuid "518e2251-cc5d-5108-bce8-18685a7d6e9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425590}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425552} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f816e4e-cb4e-5a7e-a240-55ae635308bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425650} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35f63ae3-58f0-5783-9968-b6b7f8b67885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425574} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8394aa-70c8-531a-8793-c77b8f9da3bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425606}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425574} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c2f9ef-7400-51b3-adc8-5976e8bc684f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19361797-c18f-5c79-a0bb-1599c95a5d3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425560} {:answer/id #uuid "c6cf6088-a7ab-5fa5-b537-1853d335b7b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425620}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425620} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfc29204-c5ea-57f3-b73f-d309a805b808" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63d4f703-9f1b-5e6f-b25a-56dd0791a817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425592} {:answer/id #uuid "edf7d37e-5d75-5f27-bc9f-0079cc8b3b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425633}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425633} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f9f671-11c9-5940-b954-9ff8e3b7a115" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c4b9a1ad-55e6-52d3-8f59-ef1cc199427a" :question/math-academy-id "q-342459" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & x\\in [-3,0) \\\\ {x}^{2}, & x\\in [0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | $\\lim_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/11/11f9718c9384ad2fea0bf3f5cc7da720559c512a5b3cebbc11ca966d5ec0f28b.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}2x=2(-3)=-6\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {3}^{-}}{x}^{2}=(3)^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\lim_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement III is false.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/d0/d0212ece76aba288e88b0c4d9f2e0f6163f4fd1f594cee30e9ea5f764ebc5f69.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425929 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0775b041-2fcc-5161-beb5-80cd60e4af23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474960} {:answer/id #uuid "f695d431-d46b-54df-b510-3aea6bbccfdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474961}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474960} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b9ce56f-633d-52a6-9fe3-5e31c2ec3104" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475406} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e2c39ea-ff23-5ab6-97b2-01c12343ec12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474962} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0dbf92-3cec-57d5-bf09-b54ff477f7e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474963}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474962} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cfbefaa-3aac-5745-9c77-f042b1776296" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475407} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "787b4942-1ca4-5050-825d-4ac096b82f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474964} {:answer/id #uuid "b98f4c53-ec17-539a-b8eb-fcaada4b3fa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474965}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474965} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f93c2fb-74eb-51e3-8d97-e03de7254f93" :answer-field/key "$\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1654ded7-c0bc-579c-a9e9-6daa6a1243e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-86894" :question/problem "![](images/5d/5d8f57afa16e99c13e6e36c5544a7c7594da13321bd3d01692a5a296a20953d7.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D$ and the rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/ce/ce9b9f3435a94b3f9f87b195e5b1591c80281b23cfb76ceb8e79cdeec3ae66b0.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $x{e}^{y}$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use functions $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}.\n$$ Both of these functions are not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(2,2)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the functions are nonzero at this point.\n\n- Function $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}\n$$ equals $x{e}^{y}$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}\n$$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c96195d-9858-594d-bb72-8ff337d223f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474906} {:answer/id #uuid "ac21b789-f73c-5a27-a558-3259fd8be378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474907}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474906} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeb5c3d2-18c2-5791-91fb-de36d351c3f3" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{R}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,1]\\times [-3,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ab7c8fd-5e59-504d-87ca-07f4eaf0b228" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474908} {:answer/id #uuid "e456c4ef-ec5d-5bb0-bee8-fd0487478461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474909}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474909} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc86775b-88dd-5f7c-98f3-98d7a6ccc3be" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475380} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80b9bb14-06f2-5942-afb1-747bedec4368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474910} {:answer/id #uuid "6c9391cb-f39e-56c2-b392-ee39256bc2c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474911}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186474910} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a36324a-0315-506f-92d5-cf0da1cac767" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "19ad1761-3136-5be8-b038-5aa62265f48b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80526" :question/problem "![](images/88/8866056ce5c7c80ed8452246cc3a40074b6841615ed6ef472e7a1612709e51fa.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{R}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,\n$$ where $R=[-2,1]\\times [-3,2]$” is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,\n$$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$” is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,\n$$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-2,2]$” is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,\n$$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e6eef2f-1705-5a9c-bd6f-ce326ab994cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453350} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1148f9-565b-5ed6-a20a-300c09389e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453351}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453350} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e444938-dc10-56c1-872a-deebe68ed5da" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A$ $={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,$ $\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454425} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "988b7db4-ebf6-5468-8780-b1beeb8ee195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453352} {:answer/id #uuid "02fb2d7a-770f-5219-9a76-41ff9f0fb874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453353}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453353} :answer-field/id #uuid "39570068-589a-5da0-8fe4-5a34775ee0bb" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A$ $={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,$ $\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454426} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7e357a2-e551-5cf6-8fcf-5ea5e81ecbbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453354} {:answer/id #uuid "4f50774f-f918-5ee5-90e6-3807acef4736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453355}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453354} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f26f489-8e77-5de8-9048-273b50f7f444" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{R}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A$ $={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,$ $\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-4,4]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1c04d4c5-9913-59ea-a83f-46d8bb7c02cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-129893" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}+2$ and the $x$-axis. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/3b/3bfc135232008824ae0522bcc8454c5f97c2dfd13fb6e333e146a040ccbc1f22.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+3y), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statements “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle ={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$ $\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,3]$” is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Statements “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle ={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$ $\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,2]$” is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{R}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle ={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$ $\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-4,4]$” is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$ $$\n\\displaystyle ={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$ $\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,2]$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e8a10c-8bca-5b60-94fa-c58a19413d8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426223} {:answer/id #uuid "57650fd3-48dd-55d0-ac9f-7d32e8ecc4b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426224} {:answer/id #uuid "c0132ea6-fdc2-5a17-acb2-a6b30862b933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426225} {:answer/id #uuid "c404deb2-b7c8-573d-8c43-7e7ec28f3b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426226} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b44f8c-0f09-5979-a51a-7558f4d266c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426227}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426225} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2057c9f-e99d-5d1c-a575-837b0893982e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0ee0de2e-5389-59ac-b881-e7c459d89539" :question/math-academy-id "q-158461" :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\le 0)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}(3{x}^{2}+2x+1),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 0) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{20}(3{x}^{2}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}3{x}^{2}+2x+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{[{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}([{0}^{3}+{0}^{2}+0]-[(-2)^{3}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}(0-[-8+4-2]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426267 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df195bef-be90-5b17-81c7-6ebe22d082fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426255}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426255} :answer-field/id #uuid "05bbd010-f6f1-5bf4-b78d-793dba0e386e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58a8df56-e805-5459-8255-ce8d0ce32e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426246}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426246} :answer-field/id #uuid "167f892e-c054-5442-a4a4-6b111df78980" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8043153a-4007-5470-98ef-3dcb581ee71e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426247} :answer-field/id #uuid "b327a6ea-c521-5ff3-9905-1a3b91e728ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "317b9d0c-4dca-5b66-9042-f920e2ca78b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-275499" :question/problem "A stick of length $1$ is broken at a point chosen uniformly at random along its length. Let the continuous random variable $X$ denote the distance from the left end of the stick to the break point, and let $Y=Y(X)$ denote the length of the longest piece.\n\nExpressing the integrands in the following equation as polynomials, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\text{E}[Y]={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\n$$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\text{d}x.$\n\nTherefore, the expected length of the longer piece is \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ and a function $r(x),$ the rule of the lazy statistician states that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X)]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this problem, the break point $X$ is uniformly distributed over the interval $[0,1]$, so the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x)=1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nWhen the stick is broken at point $X$, it is divided into two pieces: one of length $X$ and the other of length $1-X.$ The longer of the two pieces, $Y,$ is therefore given by\n\n$$\nY=max(X,1-X).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we define\n\n$$\nr(x)=max(x,1-x).\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the integral, we express $r(x)$ as an explicit piecewise function. Observe that,\n\n- if $0\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}$, then $x\\le 1-x$, so the longer piece has length $1-x,$\n\n- if $\\frac{1}{2}<x\\le 1$, then $x>1-x$, so the longer piece has length $x.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nr(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-x, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ x, & \\,\\frac{1}{2}<x\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & =\\text{E}[max(X,1-X)] \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(1-x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1/2}+{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2})+(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{8})+(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected length of the longer piece is $\\frac{3}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1753e041-6891-5669-bd71-7e49a240e47c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426238} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4f012b-2bdb-5642-b09a-a4c7c61052ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426239} {:answer/id #uuid "54610ec1-6556-5eea-8174-3ff6615e83d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426244} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c66ef1-332e-5a7c-8a27-02356d02c799" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426251} {:answer/id #uuid "e68b872f-6d74-52ce-a801-95a96973229a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426257}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426244} :answer-field/id #uuid "20ce458e-93f8-5c95-a799-6bfd4acd761e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9a8266f5-70f1-5e8b-ae8c-803baf5e82ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-149669" :question/problem "Find $\\text{E}[\\frac{{X}^{2}}{8}],$ given that the continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ and a function $r(x),$ the rule of the lazy statistician states that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(X)]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nr(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\frac{{X}^{2}}{8}] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-0+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f329f9a9-a752-5140-9d10-c2ac0622bcee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427232}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427232} :answer-field/id #uuid "23cb2bd7-91ba-56a2-a9d5-08480b43005c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b7dfd6b-8244-5f0b-89eb-548bcdf54c36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{x}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427219}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427219} :answer-field/id #uuid "76956d54-e511-5cce-a952-f9364f1e5f6f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c84ebae-5440-5360-8ccf-0ae76d0005c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427220}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427220} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6704cff-0378-5a2d-a8a9-c131cb49acce" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c6838816-09f0-5c1d-bec0-f98c72a4afc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-275747" :question/problem "A stick of length $4$ is broken at a point chosen uniformly at random along its length. Let the continuous random variable $X$ denote the distance from the left end of the stick to the break point, and let $Y=Y(X)$ denote the length of the longest piece.\n\nExpressing the integrands in the following equation as polynomials, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\text{E}[Y]={\\int }_{0}^{2}\n$$\n{{field-1}} $$\n\\displaystyle \\text{d}x\\,\\,+\\,\\,{\\int }_{2}^{4}\n$$\n{{field-2}} $\\text{d}x$\n\nTherefore, the expected length of the longer piece is  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ and a function $r(x)$, the rule of the lazy statistician states that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[r(x)]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\text{ }\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x)$ is the probability density function of $X.$ \n\nIn this problem, the break point $X$ is chosen uniformly from $[0,4]$, so the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\le x<4.\n$$\n\nWhen the stick is broken at point $X$, it is divided into two pieces: one of length $X$ and the other of length $4-X.$ The longer of the two pieces, $Y$, is therefore given by\n\n$$\nY=\\text{max}(X,4-X).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we define\n\n$$\nr(x)=\\text{max}(x,4-x).\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the integral, we express $r(x)$ as an explicit piecewise function. Observe that,\n\n- if $0\\le x\\le 2$, then $x\\le 4-x$, so the longer piece has length $4-x$,\n\n- if $2<x\\le 4$, then $x>4-x$, so the longer piece has length $x.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nr(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4-x, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ x, & 2<x\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & =\\text{E}[\\text{max}(X,4-X)] \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }r(x)f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[4x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(8-2)+\\frac{1}{4}(8-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4}+\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{4} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the expected length of the longer piece is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0addfc1b-9d02-54e5-8a6c-dd9cd58986f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427279} {:answer/id #uuid "17fc818e-1be8-57fa-8910-2ceb34d1bfea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427283} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb44b98-48db-57a3-ba4e-4af609be3544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427289} {:answer/id #uuid "70d02cfc-345f-501e-aae7-81b360481a06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427306} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0bfc22-7fbd-53d9-bfaf-6dd316f1bf07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427321}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427283} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea5d3c17-6171-5c4e-88bb-85a10dbabe26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "10b4599a-65d6-546d-a1db-2b8fd1bfb09d" :question/math-academy-id "q-152901" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}, & -1<x<0, \\\\ {x}^{2}, & 0\\le x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\,{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{1}{5}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(0+1)+\\frac{1}{5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{45}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18dde701-e4cf-5985-910b-d99d3686a2e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427284} {:answer/id #uuid "216706e8-4838-5204-973c-827cb86e9697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{71}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427288} {:answer/id #uuid "561a582b-3336-5381-80c8-bea3d50931a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{85}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427298} {:answer/id #uuid "5b4af875-f9cd-5e54-964a-6b3e0fd19b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{121}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427300} {:answer/id #uuid "f06289bf-091e-50d1-9b59-16cd180c1d5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{193}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427342}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427342} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c007b78-c592-57ca-92fd-6134f73345c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6e408aa1-cabb-5d40-b79a-58877a0c50b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-152921" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & 1<x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{5}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fifth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{5}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{5}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5}\\cdot (1-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{5}-{x}^{8})\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{6}\\,{x}^{6}-\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{9}){|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{24}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{9}-0)+\\frac{1}{24}(64-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{21}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{193}{72}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044244e8-f2a2-5ef1-8833-22499068eac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{53}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427277} {:answer/id #uuid "7398c53a-28aa-56f2-8f86-b9c5c3ecdfb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427307} {:answer/id #uuid "b7cc5c5a-3488-59cc-be9d-190da0ab451e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427324} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f942b5-1366-5e68-a225-6363a1b6a0c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427329} {:answer/id #uuid "f38b83dc-2a1a-5002-b5c8-92712ed90517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427343}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427277} :answer-field/id #uuid "acd8ebd9-b030-599f-8966-92f0bf6056df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6e9a565a-12f8-5f6b-b609-40f05cb5f2ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-152923" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & 0\\le x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\,x, & 1\\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fourth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{12}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{12}(64-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}+\\frac{21}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{53}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1787c976-b394-5db2-9647-7788ad9018da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427281} {:answer/id #uuid "17b6397b-6d8a-502f-b1bb-d6805bac1e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427282} {:answer/id #uuid "69257811-1577-5b8b-814f-a4ffc4c0084f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427304} {:answer/id #uuid "8386f4fd-561f-5977-a7b8-f5fa721f4d98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427313} {:answer/id #uuid "ec5e19b7-9577-599a-b29a-d5fbd4562df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427341}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427341} :answer-field/id #uuid "03eb10c9-9e29-5bb8-8db9-ad1064b9deaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "84598522-637e-5d77-b555-f1f4d414ed22" :question/math-academy-id "q-152899" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & -1<x<0, \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}\\,x, & 0\\le x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(0+1)+\\frac{1}{3}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9101a2-c4eb-5ffc-8017-56ef5d0f4631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427280} {:answer/id #uuid "74b705a1-7b7f-567b-b1a0-4e5f5a39eca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427308} {:answer/id #uuid "88154b96-2e73-5a0a-bc21-32bcd5e8f45d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427315} {:answer/id #uuid "c59c5886-4339-5c0d-ad4e-c08302875680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427330} {:answer/id #uuid "e30c5074-c231-5111-a50b-ae42316e1152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427339}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427315} :answer-field/id #uuid "a45670cd-9618-5c8d-b9e3-77951bdb7b1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9e993c85-9e06-5795-8658-efd529bfafbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-152900" :question/problem "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}\\,{x}^{3}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}\\,{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{7}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a997faa-836e-5f83-9264-4f0804fb7e52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4561" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427599} {:answer/id #uuid "538024b2-4701-5428-8d5e-360b49e72e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427601} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe5d3c3-8e7b-53fe-9eb0-ef18302db68a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4981" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427613} {:answer/id #uuid "d7027add-1387-5c0f-b716-e26792b9321e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4875" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427614} {:answer/id #uuid "f2fe171c-a45f-55be-b10d-8947252fe379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5238" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427616}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427614} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f33ee8f-8a4d-5863-8709-f1963fc40af1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1d0d65d5-ccab-55b5-8cd5-5240c8c44547" :question/math-academy-id "q-143506" :question/problem "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{55}$ be a random sample of size $n=55$ from a population with probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=0.11,$ calculate $P(1.6<\\overset{―}{X}<1.7).$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.* \n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.9783\\,$ | $\\,0.9788\\,$ | $\\,0.9793\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.9830\\,$ | $\\,0.9834\\,$ | $\\,0.9838\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.9868\\,$ | $\\,0.9871\\,$ | $\\,0.9875\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ The central limit theorem (or CLT) states that for sufficiently large $n,$ the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ can be approximated as \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case:\n\n- the sample size is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =55,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{20}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{20} \\\\  & =1.6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the population variance is ${\\sigma }^{2}=0.11.$\n\nTherefore, by the CLT, we have that the distribution of the sample mean can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}) \\\\  & ∼N\\,(1.6,\\frac{0.11}{55}) \\\\  & ∼N(1.6,0.002).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find $P(1.6<\\overset{―}{X}<1.7).$ So, we convert $\\overset{―}{X}$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1.6<\\overset{―}{X}<1.7) & =P(\\frac{1.6-1.6}{\\sqrt{0.002}}<Z<\\frac{1.7-1.6}{\\sqrt{0.002}}) \\\\  & ≈P(0<Z<2.24) \\\\  & =P(Z<2.24)-P(Z<0) \\\\  & =Φ(2.24)-Φ(0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(2.24)=0.9875,\n$$\n\nand by the symmetry of the normal distribution, $Φ(0)=0.5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1.6<\\overset{―}{X}<1.7) & =Φ(2.24)-Φ(0) \\\\  & =0.9875-0.5 \\\\  & =0.4875.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427627 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00909de5-78c6-566c-a863-78e674da4001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7486" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427594} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1bcbe5-94d2-5f8f-a591-7019c14ce8cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7734" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427602} {:answer/id #uuid "6a927ab8-2f4a-512e-9ea1-7aa6a90bb7dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7123" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427603} {:answer/id #uuid "b36d0063-601f-5e52-8869-296eadd64e20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7794" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427609} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb0feef-cf3b-531d-bbe3-c73c9cb002c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7088" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427615}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427594} :answer-field/id #uuid "35ea2e92-a991-5ad0-b8a0-bbf114233843" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cf3d34cb-ae06-547f-b3ac-ac68c79a89fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-263597" :question/problem "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{30}$ be a random sample of size $n=30$ from a population with probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=0.33,$ calculate $P(\\overset{―}{X}<1.07).$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.* \n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ | $\\,0.7123\\,$ | $\\,0.7157\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ | $\\,0.7454\\,$ | $\\,0.7486\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ | $\\,0.7794\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ The central limit theorem (or CLT) states that for sufficiently large $n,$ the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ can be approximated as \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case:\n\n- the sample size is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =30,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4}-0 \\\\  & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the population variance is ${\\sigma }^{2}=0.33.$\n\nTherefore, by the CLT, we have that the distribution of the sample mean can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}) \\\\  & ∼N\\,(1,\\frac{0.33}{30}) \\\\  & ∼N(1,0.011).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find $P(\\overset{―}{X}<1.07).$ So, we convert $\\overset{―}{X}$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}<1.07) & =P(Z<\\frac{1.07-1}{\\sqrt{0.011}}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z<0.67) \\\\  & =Φ(0.67)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.67)=0.7486.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}<1.07) & =Φ(1.07) \\\\  & =0.7486.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
